# Same Supabase project the iOS app uses. Both values are public/anon-scoped, safe to
# expose client-side (NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is required for that reason).
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://ipfzswswwukfqphloojo.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_KvH6r2_haPL1sbAc1d4F-Q_5l1ImkpK

# NOT used by auth. The sign-in page derives its callback from window.location.origin,
# because PKCE scopes the code verifier cookie to the origin that started the flow — a
# build-time constant pointing anywhere else fails every exchange. Auth origins are
# configured in Supabase instead: Auth -> URL Configuration -> Site URL (the production
# domain) and Redirect URLs (every origin that may sign in, each as .../auth/callback,
# including http://localhost:3000/auth/callback for dev). An origin missing from that
# list is silently replaced with Site URL, which is exactly how a sign-in on one domain
# ends up completing on another and losing its verifier.

# Sanity CMS (marketing copy: hero text, feature copy, FAQ entries, legal page bodies).
# Project ID is public/non-secret by design — reads go straight to Sanity's CDN API,
# no token needed, as long as the "production" dataset is Public and this app's origin
# is allowed under Sanity project settings -> API -> CORS origins. Studio itself is
# embedded at /studio (src/sanity/) — sign-in there is a real Sanity account, separate
# from this app's own Supabase auth.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_PROJECT_ID=fck477cu
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_DATASET=production
NEXT_PUBLIC_SANITY_API_VERSION=2024-01-01

# NEXT_PUBLIC_FAQ_ADMIN_SECRET used to live here: the Studio FAQ tool sent it as an x-admin-secret
# header to the `admin-faq` Edge Function. Being NEXT_PUBLIC_ it was inlined into a JS chunk served
# from /studio, a public route, so anyone who loaded that page could read it out of the bundle.
# The tool now writes to faq_entries directly as the signed-in admin, gated by the
# `faq_entries_admin_write` RLS policy, so no secret is needed. If this variable is still set in
# Vercel or a local .env, delete it, and revoke the matching FAQ_ADMIN_SECRET Supabase secret.

# RevenueCat Web Billing (RevenueCat Billing, powered by Stripe) public key — from the
# RevenueCat dashboard -> Project settings -> API keys -> "Web Billing" public key.
# Safe to expose client-side, same trust model as the app's RevenueCat public SDK key.
# The value previously hardcoded in the old static site (strp_sb_...) looked like a
# sandbox/test key — confirm/rotate for production before go-live.
NEXT_PUBLIC_REVENUECAT_WEB_BILLING_API_KEY=

# Zoho Mail SMTP — shared by /api/support (the /support page's contact form) and
# /api/waitlist (Android waitlist confirmation + notification emails), via
# lib/mail/zoho.ts. Server-only (no NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix). Same account/secrets already
# configured for the iOS app's submit-help-message Supabase function, just copied here
# rather than renamed. ZOHO_SMTP_USER/PASSWORD must be the real licensed mailbox login
# (e.g. rosa@) and an app-specific password — never an alias like support@/hello@, which
# has no password of its own and fails auth with a misleading "Authentication Failed".
ZOHO_SMTP_USER=
ZOHO_SMTP_PASSWORD=
ZOHO_SMTP_HOST=smtp.zoho.com
ZOHO_SMTP_PORT=465
ZOHO_FROM_ADDRESS=

# Who gets notified of a new Android waitlist signup (app/api/waitlist/route.ts) —
# separate from ZOHO_FROM_ADDRESS above, which is who the emails are sent *as*.
WAITLIST_NOTIFY_EMAIL=hello@twofoldapp.com.au
